// Title: PowerShell Profile Modification
// Sigma ID: b5b78988-486d-4a80-b991-930eff3ff8bf
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: HieuTT35, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-24 | Modified: 2023-10-23
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1546.013
// Description: Detects the creation or modification of a powershell profile which could indicate suspicious
//   activity as the profile can be used as a mean of persistence
// False positives:
//   - System administrator creating Powershell profile manually
// References:
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2019/05/29/turla-powershell-usage/
//   - https://persistence-info.github.io/Data/powershellprofile.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_powershell_profile.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1" or FolderPath endswith "\\PowerShell\\profile.ps1" or FolderPath endswith "\\Program Files\\PowerShell\\7-preview\\profile.ps1" or FolderPath endswith "\\Program Files\\PowerShell\\7\\profile.ps1" or FolderPath endswith "\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\profile.ps1" or FolderPath endswith "\\WindowsPowerShell\\profile.ps1"
